On 11/2/05, Matt Arnold <matt.mattarn@gmail.com> wrote:
> I would like to volunteer to be on the board or work on BPFK, wherever
> I'd be most needed.  Here is my election speech (ahem).

Members of the BPFK so far are self-selected, so you can start
as soon as you want:

"The Commission will be established by special mailing list at lojban.org.
The Board invites all Lojbanists who believe that they have demonstrated
some skill in using the language to voluntarily participate in the commission
activities. Participation will require being responsive to requests by
the Chair,
and being willing to actively seek consensus; level of participation will be
determined by the individuals. If this open membership becomes unwieldy,
or factions develop that are preventing progress, the Chair will seek a
modification of this open membership policy from the Board, but our stated
preference is to be as inclusive as possible of all Lojbanists who are willing
to help in the critical effort of cmavo list documentation."
(Taken from <http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=Official+Baseline+Statement>)

Here you can find out about goals and procedures:
<http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=baupla+fuzykamni>

To be elected as a member of the LLG Board you first need to become
a member of LLG. The latter is easy, I don't think anyone who
has expressed their interest in becoming a member has ever been
turned down, and you are certainly more than qualified. Just attend the
meeting as observer (i.e. ask Robin to add you to the llg-list) and speak
up when the election of new members comes up.

